  "classification": {
    "rootCause": "code-bug",
    "summary": "RouteProcessor2.processRoute() never checked that the pool address encoded in the user-supplied `route` was a real UniswapV3 pool, so an attacker-controlled 'pool' could call back into uniswapV3SwapCallback and make the router execute transferFrom against any wallet that had approved it."
  },
